q=json.loads((P/'benchmark-v1/questions.json').read_text());k=json.loads((P/'benchmark-v1/answer-key.json').read_text());q['benchmark_version']=k['benchmark_version']='v2-expanded'
rows=[
('How are action stacks prepared, how many cards are revealed at the start of each round, and where does the standard round marker start?','Separate stacks by backs1–5, shuffle each separately face down (eleven each in1–4, sole King in5). Reveal top of each, five total. Marker starts space1; advance one each later round.','2,3','Preparation; round marker','Distinct setup and round-start procedure'),
('After you play a power card, is it returned to hand for later rounds, and how are played cards displayed?','No, stays face up in own used stack with only top card visible; recovery special action required to retrieve one.','3,12','Play power cards; recovery','Used-card destination and information visibility'),
('If you use the King card’s special action before deploying, which King position controls deployment, and where may the King be placed?','Current new position governs adjacent destinations; special action may place King in any board region except Castillo. If deploy first, old position applies.','4,7,12','Deployment; sequence; King card','King movement changes deployment restriction with chosen order'),
('How is a Veto card retained, what can it prevent, and can it stop the ordinary deployment part of another action card?','Place it before you and retain to prevent one special action; cannot stop ordinary deployment.','9','Veto','Veto target and retention'),
('With Veto held, must other players announce special actions, when should you object, and what happens if it is partly or fully completed?','Others announce before executing. Object as soon as action begins, may veto announced action before execution; may stop only part/remainder while incomplete. Completed action cannot be vetoed.','9','Veto','Veto interruption window and partial execution'),
('When is Veto discarded after use, and when does an unused Veto expire?','After one veto discard immediately; unused discard at end of round following selection. Usable selection round or next.','9','Veto','Veto lifetime branch'),
('Who is affected by the all-court Decay of Authority card and where do those Caballeros go, including a player with an empty court?','Fellow players/opponents send all court Caballeros to provinces; actor excluded; empty court sends none.','9','Decay all','Court clearing target and zero branch'),
('For Decay of Authority requiring three from each fellow player’s court, what happens if a fellow player has two and you have five?','Opponent sends both to provinces; each opponent with fewer3 sends all court. Actor sends none and retains five.','9','Decay3','Limited court loss with shortage fallback'),
('For The King returns!, what does the detailed execution paragraph require about participants, amount, sources and order, and how does its heading differ?','Detailed paragraph says each player sends3 own Caballeros to provinces, starting actor’s left clockwise (thus actor last). Sources any regions and/or court except King’s region/Castillo. Heading says fellow players; detailed paragraph and card face say each player.','9','King returns','Distinct return action; explicit source wording discrepancy'),
('On the action sending one Caballero from each player from any region back to provinces, who chooses the pieces, does the acting player lose one, and what sources are excluded?','Actor chooses one from each player including own; region sources only, not King’s region or Castillo (not courts). Return provinces.','9','One per player','Actor selection including self; region-only return'),
('For the secret removal of two own Caballeros from a region, how do affected fellow players choose and reveal, and what region must a player with a legal region containing at least two choose?','Simultaneous secret disk choices revealed together; each affected opponent chooses one region containing at least2 own, returns2 to provinces; cannot take from King region/Castillo.','7,9','Secret Disk; remove2','Single-origin secret removal eligibility'),
('For secret removal of two, if a fellow player has at most one own Caballero in every legal region, what selection and removal is required?','Select a region containing one own Caballero and return that one to provinces; cannot take from King region or Castillo.','9','Remove2 fallback','Explicit singleton fallback'),
('For fellow players secretly returning all their own Caballeros from one region, what must the chosen region contain, how is it selected, and what if a player has no Caballeros in any region?','Simultaneous secret disks then reveal; selected legal region must contain at least1 own; return all own there to provinces; no board-region Caballeros means unaffected. King region/Castillo excluded.','7,10','Secret all return','Whole-region removal and no-board-pieces branch'),
('For the special action choosing any one location to score, may you choose the King’s region or Castillo, do ordinary scoring rules apply, and are Castillo pieces redistributed?','Yes either; ordinary Score Regions rules including applicable bonuses/rank limits. Castillo scored then covered again, not redistributed.','10,11','Choose region score','Scoring choice reaches taboo region and Castillo'),
('For scoring all 4-value regions, what value determines eligibility when mobile scoreboards are present? Specifically, Galicia has8/4/0 and Granada4/0/0: which qualifies, and do bonuses apply?','Use current mobile scoreboard’s first value instead of covered printed values; Galicia not4 so excluded, Granada4 qualifies; normal home/King bonuses apply.','10','All4 scoring','Mobile scoreboard changes category membership'),
('Which printed regions are the 5-value group and the 6-and-7-value group, how do mobile scoreboards affect these groups, and is the Castillo included in all-5 scoring?','5: Basque Country5/3/1, Aragon5/4/1, Valencia5/3/2. 6/7: Old Castile6/4/2, New Castile7/4/2, Granada6/3/1. Current mobile first value overrides printed category. Castillo not scored by all5.','10','All5; all6/7','Other explicitly selected score categories and Castillo exclusion'),
('When the first-position-only scoring card is used, what do tied leaders and lower ranks score, and is the Castillo scored?','Only sole first places score; tied first receives nothing because normally shifts to second; other ranks nothing; Castillo excluded.','11','First position only','First-only tie exception'),
('For the most-Caballeros-region scoring card, what if two board regions tie for the most total Caballeros and the Castillo contains more than either?','Both tied board regions scored normally; Castillo neither considered in comparison nor scored.','11','Most Caballeros','Max-region selection tie and castle exclusion'),
('For the least-Caballeros-region scoring card, how are empty regions, ties for least and the Castillo treated?','Ignore empty regions and Castillo, neither considered nor scored. Score all tied least nonempty board regions normally.','11','Least Caballeros','Minimum positive-region selection'),
('For the 4-stack Movement card, whose pieces leave the chosen region, how are destinations selected, and what happens to a player choosing the King’s region or the region being vacated?','Fellow players move all own Caballeros from chosen region; affected players simultaneously choose another region secretly via disks then reveal and move each group there. Either invalid choice sends that player’s pieces to own court. King’s region cannot supply pieces.','7,11','Movement','Forced movement secret resolution and invalid destination branches'),
('How far may Royal Adviser move the King, compared with the King card?','Royal Adviser at most one region away to neighboring region; King card any board region except Castillo.','11,12','Royal Adviser; King card','Distinct King movement range restriction'),
('What does The Court special action add, from where to where, and how is this separate from a 4-stack card’s normal deployment?','Adds2 own Caballeros provinces to court; normal card allows up to4 court to board adjacent King and/or Castillo; two complete activities in either order.','7,11,12','4-stack; Court; sequence','Court replenishment special and deployment ordering'),
('On the action where each player secretly chooses a region to score, how are choices made/revealed and how are duplicate and unique selections resolved?','All secretly choose using disks simultaneously then reveal together; score uniquely selected regions under normal rules; a region chosen by multiple players not scored.','7,12','Secret scoring','Simultaneous score selection collisions'),
('For Intrigue moving all your own Caballeros from one region, can you split them and leave some in the original region, and what origin/destination restrictions apply?','Take all own from one non-King region; distribute among other non-King regions and/or Castillo; some may return to original region. No taking from Castillo.','7,8','All own from one','Single-origin own relocation with explicit return exception'),
('With Intrigue adding two more Caballeros from court, how many may be added including normal deployment, and how do the two destination allowances differ?','Up to3 total: special2 from court to any non-King regions and/or Castillo; normal1 from court only adjacent King and/or Castillo.','8','Two more from court','Extra deployment has broader destination scope'),
('For the Intrigue choice card offering two additional court Caballeros OR all own Caballeros from one region, may you execute both special alternatives, and what normal deployment remains?','Choose one special alternative, not both; ordinary up-to1 court placement adjacent King and/or Castillo remains. May decline special altogether.','7,8','Either/or Intrigue','Exclusive special-action alternatives'),
('For Intrigue moving up to five Caballeros from any one region, may they have different owners or come from multiple origin regions, and where can they go?','Up to5 own and/or foreign but all one origin region; not King region/Castillo origin; distribute any non-King regions and/or Castillo.','7,8','Up to5 one region','Mixed ownership but single-origin limit'),
('For Intrigue moving any three foreign Caballeros, may you choose fewer or use multiple origins, can your own pieces be included, and what destinations are legal?','Up to3 foreign only, from any multiple non-King regions, not Castillo; any non-King regions and/or Castillo destinations. Own excluded.','7,8','3 foreign','Foreign-only multi-origin relocation'),
('For Intrigue moving any three Caballeros on the board, what is the ownership and origin flexibility, maximum, and destination restriction?','Up to3 own and/or foreign, from any non-King regions (not Castillo), to any non-King regions and/or Castillo.','7,8','Any3','Three-any mixed ownership relocation'),
('For Intrigue moving two of yours and two foreign Caballeros, what are the separate ownership allowances, may multiple origin regions be used, and what locations are forbidden as sources or allowed as destinations?','Up to2 own and up to2 foreign, multiple non-King region origins; no King/Castillo source. Destinations any non-King regions and/or Castillo.','7,8','2 own2 foreign','Separate ownership quotas cannot substitute for each other'),
('For Intrigue moving any four of your own Caballeros, what maximum/ownership and origin/destination restrictions apply?','Up to4 own only from any non-King regions (not Castillo), to other non-King regions and/or Castillo.','7,8','4 own','Four-own-only allowance'),
('For Intrigue moving any four Caballeros, what maximum/ownership and origin/destination restrictions apply?','Up to4 own and/or foreign, any non-King region origins (not Castillo), to other non-King regions and/or Castillo.','7,8','4 any','Four-any mixed allowance')]
for i,(question,answer,pages,section,novelty) in enumerate(rows,21):
 id=f'Q{i:02}';q['questions'].append({'id':id,'question':question});k['answers'].append({'id':id,'expected_answer':answer,'source_references':[{'path':'extracted/el-grande-rules.txt','pdf_pages':pages,'section':section}],'novelty':novelty})
